  "profileFaqScreenTitle": "FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS",
  "profileFaqQuestion1": "How do I import a character from aidedd.org?",
  "profileFaqAnswer1": "On aidedd.org, open your character sheet and use its XML export (the site's export button). In Nexus JDR, go to the Characters list and tap \"Import XML\" at the bottom of the screen, next to \"+ Create\", then select that .xml file. The app automatically pre-fills the sheet (stats, class, race, spells, inventory...) and shows you a review screen before saving it, with a badge on any fields it couldn't recognize so you can fill them in yourself.",
  "profileFaqQuestion2": "How do I join my GM's story?",
  "profileFaqAnswer2": "Your GM sends you an invitation link from the Histoires app. On Android, open that link on your phone: Nexus JDR opens on the invitation (sign in first if needed, you then land back on it). The app shows you the story's name and the GM's name; by joining, your character becomes visible to the GM in read-only mode, and you can leave the story at any time from its sheet. You then pick the character to attach, or create a new one. The app does not send an invitation notification and does not offer manual code entry for now; opening the link in the app is not yet available on iPhone/iPad.",
  "profileFaqQuestion3": "Are my characters saved offline?",
  "profileFaqAnswer3": "Mostly. Without a connection you can view your list and the sheets you have already opened, and edit hit points (and temporary HP), XP, spell slots, innate spells, features, conditions, rest, prepared spells, equipped or attuned items, inspiration, AC bonus, currency, journal and inventory (custom item, removal, use, loot). These changes are held on your device, then sent automatically when the network is back. Only one rest is held at a time per character: until it is sent, a second rest is refused; wait until you're back online. To add a catalog item offline, open the catalog at least once while online; a custom item always works. The banner at the top of the screen shows the status: \"Offline\", \"N changes pending\" or \"Synced\". If the same sheet was edited on another device, an alert tells you; your offline change is applied on top. Still needing a connection: character creation, level-up, marking dead or reviving, archiving or deleting a character, character story, pact weapon, portrait, sharing, groups, XML import and export, account deletion and bug reports.",
  "profileFaqQuestion4": "How does leveling up work?",
  "profileFaqAnswer4": "From the character sheet, the \"Level up\" screen guides you step by step: new hit points, unlocked class features, new spell slots if your class casts spells, and an ability score increase if the level allows it. Nothing is applied until you confirm the summary screen.",
  "profileFaqQuestion5": "How do I change my character's portrait?",
  "profileFaqAnswer5": "Open the character sheet, tap its portrait, then choose \"Take a photo\" or \"Choose from gallery\". You can then crop the image before saving it — it's stored securely and linked only to that character.",
  "profileFaqQuestion6": "How do I delete my account?",
  "profileFaqAnswer6": "From Profile > Privacy & data > Delete my account, at the bottom of the screen (danger zone). This action is irreversible: it permanently deletes your characters, their portraits and all links to stories. You can export your data before confirming.",

